NUM-52: make the PID controller a plain velocity-form PID (no error reset, no dead band)

getPIDSetting() zeroed the stored errors e1 and e2 whenever the error had not
changed by 0.0001 since the last evaluation. With a steady error the next
update then used e1 = 0, so the proportional term added kp*e (and the
derivative term kd*e/dt) at every evaluation: a P-only controller with a
constant error drove its link to 0 or 1 at a rate set by the routing step.
The reset existed to unstick the controller after the 0.0001 dead band on
each update had thrown away small increments, which in the velocity form are
lost for good (a PI controller with a small steady error never removes it).
Remove both, so the setting moves by kp*[(e0 - e1) + e0*dt/ki + kd*(...)/dt]
at every evaluation as the equation says.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-52_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/controls.c b/src/legacy/engine/controls.c
index e423886..9b9f090 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/controls.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/controls.c
@@ -1660,7 +1660,6 @@ double getPIDSetting(struct TAction *a, double dt)
 {
     double e0, setting;
     double p, i, d, update;
-    double tolerance = 0.0001;
 
     // --- convert time step from days to minutes
     dt *= 1440.0;
@@ -1675,13 +1674,6 @@ double getPIDSetting(struct TAction *a, double dt)
             e0 = e0 / ControlValue;
     }
 
-    // --- reset previous errors to 0 if controller gets stuck
-    if (fabs(e0 - a->e1) < tolerance)
-    {
-        a->e2 = 0.0;
-        a->e1 = 0.0;
-    }
-
     // --- use the recursive form of the PID controller equation to
     //     determine the new setting for the controlled link
     p = (e0 - a->e1);
@@ -1691,8 +1683,6 @@ double getPIDSetting(struct TAction *a, double dt)
         i = e0 * dt / a->ki;
     d = a->kd * (e0 - 2.0 * a->e1 + a->e2) / dt;
     update = a->kp * (p + i + d);
-    if (fabs(update) < tolerance)
-        update = 0.0;
     setting = Link[a->link].targetSetting + update;
 
     // --- update previous errors
